\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Hybrid deliberative/reactive mission behavior tree. The reactive layer re-evaluates battery and interrupt conditions every tick and can preempt navigation (canceling the active Nav2 goal); the deliberative branch resolves semantic commands through the TOSM mediator, which hot-reloads the knowledge graph when the management console edits it.}}{23}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bttree}{{15}{23}{Hybrid deliberative/reactive mission behavior tree. The reactive layer re-evaluates battery and interrupt conditions every tick and can preempt navigation (canceling the active Nav2 goal); the deliberative branch resolves semantic commands through the TOSM mediator, which hot-reloads the knowledge graph when the management console edits it}{figure.15}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Semantic-goal navigation of the AMMR proxy in the Gazebo twin of the test room (world, map, and knowledge graph share the exploration-scan frame). Blue: a gated three-mission run (TV $\rightarrow $ seating area $\rightarrow $ home). Red dashed: against the pre-feedback graph the robot drives toward a verified-phantom keyboard --- a fluorescent lamp; crosses mark the three phantom goals with their failure modes (pointless drive, false arrival, unreachable). All three are refused once structure filtering and owner feedback are applied.}}{23}{figure.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:semnav}{{16}{23}{Semantic-goal navigation of the AMMR proxy in the Gazebo twin of the test room (world, map, and knowledge graph share the exploration-scan frame). Blue: a gated three-mission run (TV $\rightarrow $ seating area $\rightarrow $ home). Red dashed: against the pre-feedback graph the robot drives toward a verified-phantom keyboard --- a fluorescent lamp; crosses mark the three phantom goals with their failure modes (pointless drive, false arrival, unreachable). All three are refused once structure filtering and owner feedback are applied}{figure.16}{}}
